{
  "format": "veyq-expenses-v1-vectors",
  "note": "Conformance vectors for the Expenses entry format v1 (contracts/expenses/entry.v1.schema.json, ADR 0108 decisions 5 and 9, docs/apps/expenses.md § Entries and § What the client computes), so every client computes the same balance from the same entries. `conversion`: an entry's total into the base currency, round_half_away_from_zero(amount * rate * 10^(baseMinorUnits - minorUnits)). `rounding`: the largest-remainder allocation of an integer `total` by `weights` (exact fractions as strings), people in join order, `expected` per person in that order; its last two totals are the largest amount the schema takes, so every `total * weight` passes 2^53 and a floating-point division anywhere in the allocation gets one of them wrong. `pots`: whole Pots — participants, the current revision of each entry (the `body` minus `v` and `heads`, which carry no arithmetic), and per entry and per Pot what every client must compute, `settleUp` in the order the transfers are suggested. A Pot's `invalid`, where it has one, lists entries every client counts nowhere and shows as invalid, each with the reason (`problem`) this client names it by. Generated by an independent Python implementation (fractions.Fraction, decimal.Decimal) from the rules as the schema states them, which also re-checked `conversion` and `rounding`.",
